# Prettier formats what the repository OWNS. Everything below is either
# generated, vendored, or a scratch checkout that is not part of the tree.
#
# `.claude/worktrees/` is here for the same reason it is in `eslint.config.mjs`:
# a worktree is a full checkout of this repository nested inside it. Formatting
# one rewrites an agent's in-flight work behind its back, and a single scratch
# checkout accounted for 1186 of the 1187 files `pnpm format:check` complained
# about — which means the check had stopped being able to say anything about
# the code it exists to judge.

# `pnpm-lock.yaml` is the second case, and a quieter one: it is not scratch, it
# is the file `AGENTS.md` names when it says no lock file may be edited by hand.
# Its owner is pnpm, and pnpm 12 writes single-quoted keys where prettier wants
# double. The two cannot both be right, and the tie is not a matter of taste:
# prettier's only remedy is `--write`, which produces a lockfile pnpm has never
# emitted — and the next `pnpm install` rewrites it, so the gate fails again on
# whatever branch touched a dependency. Verified: `pnpm install --lockfile-only`
# reproduces the committed bytes exactly, and prettier still rejects them.
#
# Ignoring it keeps `format:check` able to say something. Left in, it is the one
# file that can turn a green pipeline red for a change that is not a style
# change, which is the failure mode a formatting gate exists to prevent.
# `Cargo.lock` needs no entry: prettier infers no parser for it and skips it.

# `packages/frontend-preferences/frontend-support.json` is the third case, and
# the most mechanical one. Its owner is `tooling/scripts/render-wrangler-config.mjs`,
# which writes it with `JSON.stringify(…, null, 2)`; prettier formats a short
# array onto one line. The two disagree on every render, so a format check over
# it fails as soon as the renderer has run and passes as soon as it has not —
# which is to say the gate would be reporting the order two tools happened to
# run in, not anything about the code. Same remedy as the lock file: leave the
# owner's bytes alone and keep `format:check` able to say something.
packages/frontend-preferences/frontend-support.json

